 new squares appear. That matches 48 added cells of colour 8 (6 × 8).\n- **Pair 2:**\n  - The squares use start rows {3, 8, 15} and start columns {2, 6, 12}, which gives 9 crossings.\n  - 5 are occupied, so 4 new squares appear. That matches 32 added cells.\n\nSo the rule is simply: take the set of all start rows and the set of all start columns used by the squares, and fill every empty combination with the motif in colour 8.\n\n**Query input:**\n- Start rows are {1, 6, 12, 16} and start columns are {2, 7, 11, 17, 21}, which gives 20 crossings.\n- 8 crossings already hold squares, so 12 new colour-8 squares are stamped.\n- The program fills one grid row of squares at a time and emits after each row.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    out = g.copy()\n    emit(out, \"Input: hollow squares on one column and one row of positions.\")\n    tmpl = objs[0][\"grid\"] != bg\n    h, w = tmpl.shape\n    ys = sorted({o[\"box\"][0] for o in objs})\n    xs = sorted({o[\"box\"][1] for o in objs})\n    occupied = {(o[\"box\"][0], o[\"box\"][1]) for o in objs}\n    for y in ys:\n        changed = False\n        for x in xs:\n            if (y, x) in occupied:\n                continue\n            region = out[y:y+h, x:x+w]\n            region[tmpl] = 8\n            changed = True\n        if changed:\n            emit(out, f\"Stamp colour-8 copies at every empty column position in square-row y={y}.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid: every row/column crossing holds a square.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"used by a square in the column and each x used by a square in the row, a copy of the same square is stamped there in colour 8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"ows and the set of all start columns used by the squares, and fill every empty combination with the motif in colour 8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- 8 crossings already hold squares, so 12 new colour-8 squares are stamped."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"9b795b6d7e450d8bfe1b62b2fc50213027ee804183e96e309373dfa20b32209e","task_sha256":"d4b7986b63850054ef4b534d5176d903f766ede5403aca54b9d4842f376e0a16","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
